class QgsDropFeedbackOverlay : QWidget
{
%Docstring(signature="appended")
Tells the user, over the widget they are dragging data onto, what
dropping it would do.

Only a payload worth a warning is announced: one which would replace the
project, and one nothing in QGIS can read. Anything else drops without
ceremony, and the overlay hides itself.

The overlay covers the widget it is a child of and follows its size, so
it belongs on the widget whose whole surface the message is about. It is
hidden until :py:func:`~announce` is called and hides again on
:py:func:`~clear`.

.. versionadded:: 4.4
%End

%TypeHeaderCode
#include "qgsdropfeedbackoverlay.h"
%End
  public:
    explicit QgsDropFeedbackOverlay( QWidget *parent /TransferThis/ );
%Docstring
Constructor for QgsDropFeedbackOverlay, covering ``parent``.
%End

    void announce( Qgis::DropPayloadType payloadType, const QString &name = QString() );
%Docstring
Announces that dropping data of the given ``payloadType`` is about to
happen, naming it ``name`` in the message when one is known, such as the
file being dragged.

Shows the overlay when the payload is one the user should be warned
about, and hides it otherwise.
%End

    void clear();
%Docstring
Hides the overlay, once the drag it was announcing is over.
%End

  protected:
    virtual void paintEvent( QPaintEvent *event );

    virtual bool eventFilter( QObject *watched, QEvent *event );


};

